    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/12/saucony-endorphin-elite-2-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length IncrediRUN foam is extremely soft/compliant with strong impact protection, with a very plush heel and a more controlled-bounce forefoot transition.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is high and very bouncy, especially at heel rebound, but the foam rebounds slower than snappy racers, feeling better for half/marathon efforts than faster paces.",
        "Stability: The carbon-plated build is stiff, but overall stability is limited by the very soft midsole, no rigid heel counter, and weaker lateral/side-to-side support (especially when cornering).",
        "Durability: Durability expectation is described as average, with no standout evidence of exceptional outsole or upper longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/12/saucony-endorphin-elite-2-multi-tester.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The IncrediRun TPEE foam is repeatedly described as exceptionally soft (\"softest\" tested) with a high 39.5/31.5 mm stack, giving strong impact protection and a very plush heel/forefoot feel without becoming mushy in use.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is described as very quick with strong rebound; the carbon plate contributes smooth propulsion and fast turnover, though some may want a firmer, sharper pop for short efforts.",
        "Stability: Despite very soft foam, stability is reported as better than expected due to plate integration, deep sidewalls, medial support structure, and secure rear hold; lateral/lockdown confidence is high for many but midfoot/forefoot lockdown can be finicky for some foot shapes.",
        "Durability: This excerpt gives limited long-term durability evidence (no outsole wear data); upper components (stiff toe bumper/supportive overlays) appear robust, but material longevity is not yet clearly established."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/saucony-endorphin-elite-2-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The incrediRun midsole is notably soft and squishy at easy effort, and the 39.5 mm heel / 31.5 mm forefoot stack gives a highly cushioned, protective feel over longer runs.",
        "Responsiveness: Bounce and energy return are a major strength; the foam compresses and rebounds noticeably, then feels firmer and punchier at faster paces for snappy turnover.",
        "Stability: Straight-line stability is generally fine, but the high, soft platform can feel less secure in tight corners or lateral transitions; the heel collar adds some structure, though one reviewer noted slight ankle-collar gaping.",
        "Durability: The thin PWRTRAC outsole is described as very grippy in wet and dry conditions, with no issues reported through roughly 60 miles, but long-term outsole/upper wear is not yet established."
      ]
    }
